      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-ci-diet\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/v/dsh-ci-diet.svg\" alt=\"npm version\"></a>\n  <a href=\"LICENSE\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue.svg\" alt=\"license: MIT\"></a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/0disoft/dsh-ci-diet/actions/workflows/ci.yml\"><img src=\"https://github.com/0disoft/dsh-ci-diet/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg\" alt=\"CI\"></a>\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "CI Diet",
      "text": "**Find GitHub Actions jobs that run longer or more often than they need to. Review small YAML fixes before applying them.**\n\nCI Diet is an alpha CLI and DeepSeek Harness (DSH) plugin. It reads workflow definitions and, when enabled, GitHub Actions history; then it shows findings and prepares narrow YAML edits without changing a workflow on its own."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "The CLI requires Node `^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0`. This is the current npm release, `0.5.2`.\n\n```bash\nnpm install --global dsh-ci-diet@0.5.2\nci-diet --version\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-ci-diet@0.5.2\ndsh --profile web\n\nThe plugin registers DSH tools plus the **Settings → CI Diet** and **CI Diet review** screens. Installation alone does not scan a repository, save runner minutes, or modify a workflow. If you skip the global CLI install, use `npx dsh-ci-diet@0.5.2` in place of `ci-diet`."
    },
    {
      "section": "First scan and history",
      "text": "Run these commands from the repository you want to inspect. The static scan is offline and saves its report. History sync is a separate network step that reads recent runs and jobs through the authenticated `gh` CLI using read-only GitHub API requests.\n\n```bash\nci-diet scan --cwd .\ngh auth status\nci-diet sync --cwd . --network\nci-diet report --cwd ."
    },
    {
      "section": "First scan and history",
      "text": "`gh` needs read access to the repository's Actions runs and jobs. CI Diet never needs GitHub write access. The HTML report is one self-contained file with inline CSS, no scripts, and no external requests. In DSH, `ci_diet_scan` and `ci_diet_sync` both save reports; network access and preflight are on by default for new plugin profiles."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it finds",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"docs/assets/settings-preview.png\" alt=\"CI Diet settings in English, with preflight and history analysis enabled\" width=\"820\">\n</p>\n<p align=\"center\"><sub>Settings → CI Diet. Preflight and history analysis are enabled by default.</sub></p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it finds",
      "text": "| Rule | Default | Looks for | Usual output |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| CD001 | on | PR runs superseded by a newer commit | `concurrency` plan |\n| CD002 | on | overlapping or duplicate trigger candidates | explanation |\n| CD003 | off | heavy checks for declared docs-only changes | explanation |\n| CD004 | on | large, resolvable matrices | review note |\n| CD005 | off | jobs without a timeout | measured `timeout-minutes` plan |\n| CD006 | on | supported npm, pnpm, or Bun frozen-install jobs without an explicit cache | download-cache plan |\n| CD008 | on | artifact retention longer than needed | `retention-days` plan with human attestation |"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it finds",
      "text": "CD003 and CD005 are disabled by default. CD002, CD003, and CD004 do not produce patches. CD005 caps abnormal runs; it does not shorten normal execution. CD008 changes artifact storage retention, not runner minutes. Every plan remains a hypothesis until you review it and measure the result."
    },
    {
      "section": "Supported npm cache example",
      "text": "CD006 recognizes a narrow shape: a supported `actions/setup-node@v7` step followed by `npm ci`, with a tracked manifest and lockfile. The plan adds cache inputs only; versions, installation, and tests stay in place. The example assumes `package.json` does not declare npm in either `packageManager` or `devEngines.packageManager`; v7 enables caching automatically when npm is declared, so CI Diet does not propose a redundant cache.\n\n**Before**"
    },
    {
      "section": "Supported npm cache example",
      "text": "```yaml\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n\n**After**\n\n```yaml\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n\nFor a plan command, `--step 1` means the second step in this YAML array: checkout is step `0`, setup-node is step `1`. It is a zero-based index, not a step label. See the [plugin guide](docs/guide/plugin.md) for pnpm, Bun, timeouts, retention, and current guards."
    },
    {
      "section": "Review before write",
      "text": "The workflow is **scan → preview → human approval → apply → measure**. The model tools, including `ci_diet_plan`, preview edits and compute a plan digest; they cannot approve, apply, or revert. The review screen can approve, apply, and revert after a person types the plan digest suffix or change ID. Local writes are byte-range edits to one existing workflow file."
    },
    {
      "section": "Review before write",
      "text": "```bash\nci-diet plan --cwd . --rule CD006 --workflow .github/workflows/ci.yml --job test --step 1\nci-diet plans --cwd . --plan PLAN_ID\nci-diet approve --cwd . --plan PLAN_ID --confirm CONFIRMATION\nci-diet apply --cwd . --plan PLAN_ID"
    },
    {
      "section": "Review before write",
      "text": "Approval authorizes only that plan. Apply creates a backup, rewrites the planned bytes, and performs source, dependency, policy, digest, lock, and backup checks. Revert restores the backup. CI Diet does not commit, push, deploy, run a workflow, change branch protection, or delete artifacts."
    },
    {
      "section": "Measurement and limits",
      "text": "- No savings are claimed before measurement. A finding can be wrong when history or workflow attribution is incomplete.\n- A dependency cache can add restore/save time. Its overhead can exceed the installation time it avoids; compare compatible cold and warm runs and include cache steps.\n- `measure` compares selected real runs and reports observed runner-time differences, success and rerun rates. The comparison covers those samples only; it does not establish the cause of a change or reproduce your bill.\n- The Settings page stores tool configuration and shows session-scoped reports and plans. It does not optimize a workflow by itself.\n- Source hashes, approval expiry, and policy checks can block an edit. Review the report, the diff, and the repository's own checks before keeping a change."
    },
    {
      "section": "Measurement and limits",
      "text": "| Measure | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `observedRunnerSeconds` | Runner time observed in the collected runs |\n| `modeledRoundedMinutes` | Per-job minutes rounded up; an estimate only |\n| `listPriceUsd` | List-price estimate from the embedded pricing snapshot |\n| `actualBilledUsd` | `unknown` until an actual bill can be proven |\n\nKeeping these values separate prevents modeled minutes from becoming a billing claim."
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation",
      "text": "| Need | Read |\n| --- | --- |\n| Installation, settings, CLI, review, and measurement | [Plugin guide](docs/guide/plugin.md) · [measurement section](docs/guide/plugin.md#measuring-an-applied-change) |\n| Normative product and contract map | [Specification index](docs/spec/README.md) |\n| Rule guards, cost model, patches, and storage | [Rules](docs/spec/rules.md) · [cost model](docs/spec/cost-model.md) · [patch model](docs/spec/patch-model.md) · [storage](docs/spec/storage.md) |\n| A real cache-overhead measurement | [2026-10-25 cache review](docs/measurements/2026-10-25-cache-review.md) |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation",
      "text": "<details>\n<summary>Plugin defaults, migration, and compatibility</summary>\n\nNew DSH profiles enable `preflightEnabled`, `networkEnabled`, `localApplyEnabled`, and rules CD001, CD002, CD004, CD006, and CD008. The one-time migration records `defaultsRevision: 2`; later switch and rule choices survive restarts. CD003 and CD005 stay off until explicitly enabled. State paths, retention, quotas, and existing billing inputs are preserved."
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation",
      "text": "The plugin targets DSH `>=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0` and `>=0.2.2-rc.1 <0.3.0-0`. DSH `0.3.0` is not supported. Plugin preflight checks supported deployment commands before they run, but it makes no network request or file change and skips opaque shells. CLI history requires `--network`; the plugin network switch permits `gh` calls only when the sync tool is invoked. Update with the same commands and `@latest`, then restart DSH.\n\n</details>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Contributing and license",
